## Bare Runtime Modules

These are **npm packages** — they must be installed explicitly. Unlike Node.js,
Bare has no built-in standard library. If you `import` a `bare-*` module without
installing it, you'll get `MODULE_NOT_FOUND`.

| Package | Version | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `bare-process` | `^4.3.0` | `process` equivalent (pid, argv, env, exit) |
| `bare-fs` | `^4.5.5` | File system operations |
| `bare-path` | `^3.0.0` | Path manipulation |
| `bare-crypto` | `^1.13.4` | Cryptographic primitives |
| `bare-encoding` | `^1.0.3` | TextEncoder / TextDecoder for Bare |
| `bare-buffer` | `^3.5.0` | Buffer implementation for Bare |
| `bare-subprocess` | `^5.2.2` | Child process spawning |
| `bare-env` | `^3.0.0` | Environment variable access |
| `bare-net` | `^2.2.0` | TCP / IPC sockets |
| `bare-console` | `^6.1.0` | Console API |
| `bare-os` | `^3.7.1` | OS info (platform, arch, homedir) |

## Mobile (Expo + Bare) — validate as a compatible set

Validate these versions together. A QVAC/Bare-kit update can retain Expo/RN when their requirements still match; an Expo major update requires its matching React Native and Expo package set.

The bundler is now **`bare-pack@^2.2.1`** (the 2.x line). `@qvac/sdk@0.21`
depends on `bare-pack@^2.0.1` internally, so the app and the SDK share the 2.x
toolchain (they dedupe to a single `bare-pack` in the lockfile). The 2.x CLI
replaced `--target <triple>` (removed in `bare-pack@2.0.0`, Jan 2026) with
`--host <triple>`; the `build:bare` script in
`packages/cli/src/generators/expo-mobile.ts` uses `--host` accordingly. The
host triples themselves are unchanged.

> **Mobile remains deferred.** The 9 October compatibility candidate pairs QVAC SDK 0.21.0 with Bare kit 0.15.6 (Bare 1.33.4), Expo 54 and RN 0.81.5. Native build and simulator checks are recorded separately from physical-device real inference. See `planning/status/public-launch-mobile-20261009.md` for acceptance.

| Package | Version | Why |
|---------|---------|-----|
| `bare-pack` | `^2.2.1` | Bundler. Matches `@qvac/sdk@0.21`'s internal `bare-pack@^2.0.1`; 2.x uses `--host` (not `--target`). |
| `expo` | `~54.0.33` | Pairs cleanly with `react-native@0.81.x`. **Kept on SDK 54** — the QVAC bump does not require Expo 55/56 (RN 0.83/0.85), which are a separate migration. |
| `expo-build-properties` | `~1.0.9` | Matches Expo SDK 54. Must be in `dependencies`, not just `app.json` plugins. |
| `expo-router` | `~6.0.23` | Matches Expo SDK 54. |
| `expo-file-system` | `^19.0.15` | Matches Expo SDK 54 (also the optional peer of `@qvac/sdk` for model caching). |
| `expo-device` | `~8.0.10` | Matches Expo SDK 54. Used to detect simulator vs physical device for QVAC. |
| `expo-linking` | `~8.0.11` | Required transitively by `expo-router/build/views/Unmatched.js`. |
| `expo-splash-screen` | `~31.0.10` | Matches Expo SDK 54. |
| `expo-status-bar` | `~3.0.8` | Matches Expo SDK 54. |
| `react-native` | `0.81.5` (exact) | Exact pin — Expo SDK 54 ships this. |
| `react` / `react-dom` | `19.1.0` (exact) | Matching pair prevents expo-router optional web peers from selecting an incompatible newer React DOM. |
| `react-native-bare-kit` | `0.15.6` (exact) | Hosts the Bare runtime inside RN; ships a specific runtime that must match `@qvac/sdk`'s worker bundle. `@qvac/sdk@0.21` declares it as an **optional `*` peer** (no longer an exact requirement), so we track it to the runtime verified by the SDK (Bare 1.33.4) and keep the exact pin ourselves. |
| `react-native-safe-area-context` | `~5.6.0` | Matches Expo SDK 54. |
| `react-native-screens` | `~4.16.0` | Matches Expo SDK 54. |
| `bare-rpc` | `^1.3.2` | `1.3.2+` works (covered by caret). |
| `bare-fs` | resolved transitively | **No override.** The old `bare-fs@4.5.1` exact override existed only for the `bare-pack@1.5.1` pipeline. On 2.x we let it resolve to satisfy `@qvac/sdk@0.21`'s `bare-fs@^4.5.1` (verify the installed version and engines.bare). |
| `corestore` | `^7.13.0` | Lower-bound floor — caret covers latest. |
| `hyperbee` | `^2.27.3` | Lower-bound floor — caret covers latest. |
| Node.js (build host) | `≥ 22.17` | Expo SDK 54 + `bare-pack` 2.x toolchain. |

**Rule:** retain native build and simulator evidence for the complete installed graph after a runtime update. Physical-device AI is a separate gate; keep mobile deferred until its declared support combinations pass.

